The schema tests all pass (56 tests). The wallet-service spec fails because the `WalletService` constructor imports `TigerBeetleAccountService` as a default, and when it tries to create the default instance, it connects to TigerBeetle which isn't available in the test environment.

The issue is that even though the tests pass mocks for all three repos, the `WalletService` constructor still evaluates the default imports. Looking at the code:

```ts
constructor(
    accountRepo?: IAccountRepository,
    transactionRepo?: ITransactionRepository,
    ledgerRepo?: ILedgerRepository,
  ) {
    this.accountRepo = accountRepo ?? new TigerBeetleAccountService();
    this.transactionRepo = transactionRepo ?? new TransactionRepository();
    this.ledgerRepo = ledgerRepo ?? new LedgerRepository();
  }
```

The problem is that `import { TigerBeetleAccountService } from "@/lib/tigerbeetle"` is executed at module load time, and the module likely tries to connect to TigerBeetle during initialization.

Let me check the TigerBeetle module to understand the initialization issue.

